## BATCH 2 — CRITICAL CORRECTION: there are TWO layout engines, and I audited the wrong one first

This is the most important finding in the registry so far, and it **retracts six of my own P0 items**. Read before assigning any Wave-2 work.

### What I found

`miniandroid/src/resources/layout_inflater.cpp` is **5,713 lines / 320 KB** and contains a **real, honest AOSP MeasureSpec-based layout engine** — not just an inflater. Verified by direct read at `main @ 4ada9e3e4847`:

```cpp
// :2888-2892  — real MeasureSpec decode + recursive measure with memo
auto decode = [](int w) -> MeasureSpec2 {
    return MeasureSpec2{w & 0x3FFFFFFF, (MeasureMode)(((uint32_t)w) >> 30)};
};
measure_node(views, vid, decode(wspec_word), decode(hspec_word), 0);

// :2885-2887  — memo invalidation on dirty layout
// R-NEW-302 companion: a dirty layout invalidates remembered (view, spec)
// results — the memo must not replay stale geometry.
if (views->layout_dirty) m3_measure_memo_.clear();

// :3881-3882  — getChildMeasureSpec equivalent (padding + margins subtracted)
csw = child_spec(sw, hpad + cn->lp_margin_left + cn->lp_margin_right, cw_);
csh = child_spec(sh, vpad + cn->lp_margin_top  + cn->lp_margin_bottom, ch_);

// :3885-3897  — ScrollView AND HorizontalScrollView UNSPECIFIED axis
if (n->class_desc.find("ScrollView;") != std::string::npos &&
    n->class_desc.find("Horizontal") == std::string::npos)
    csh = {std::max(0, sh.size - vpad), M_UNSPEC};
if (n->class_desc.find("HorizontalScrollView") != std::string::npos)
    csw = {std::max(0, sw.size - hpad), M_UNSPEC};
```

**LinearLayout weight law — exact AOSP port, including negative excess:**
```cpp
// :4753-4767
// ── G04 §9: AOSP LinearLayout weight law, EXACT port ────
// (LinearLayout.java @android-14 L1385-1445 measureHorizontal;
//  sequential share distribution with remainingWeightSum
//  decrement — NOT one division by the total).
//   remainingExcess = size − mTotalLength   (may be negative →
//                             weighted children SHRINK)
//   remainingWeightSum = weightSum > 0 ? weightSum : totalWeight
//   per weighted child (in order):
//     share = (int)(childWeight * remainingExcess / remainingWeightSum)
//     remainingExcess −= share; remainingWeightSum −= childWeight
//     main size = (lp == 0) ? share : measuredBase + share   [≥ 0]
```

**GridLayout — real constraint solver, not a table:**
```cpp
// :2898-2905
// ── LAYOUT-PIPE-001 (#606 FINAL): the AOSP Axis constraint law ──
// (GridLayout.java computeLinks + solve — honest port). The grid lines are
// the MINIMAL solution of two arc families:
//   • span-1 cells:      line[i+1] ≥ line[i] + trackMax[i]   (leading arcs)
//   • spanned children:  line[max]  ≥ line[min] + size      (interval arcs)
// Bellman-Ford over these forward-only arcs: forward relaxation iterated to
// a fixpoint (≤ n passes — every arc points forward).
// :4376-4378  E-wave (#606 FINAL): the REAL AOSP constraint solve
//             replaces the D-wave even-split simplification
```

**RelativeLayout anchor rules ARE parsed and stored:**
```cpp
// :2002-2004
if      (n == "layout_below")     a.rel_below    = nm;
else if (n == "layout_above")     a.rel_above    = nm;
else if (n == "layout_toRightOf") a.rel_right_of = nm;
// :1970-1971, :2037  alignParentBottom / alignParentTop / alignParentLeft
```

**weightSum IS honoured:** `:1672` `a.weight_sum = atof(raw); a.weight_sum_valid = true;` → `:2195` `node.weight_sum = a.weight_sum;`
**scaleType IS parsed with correct AOSP ordinals:** `:1894-1908` `matrix 0, fitXY 1, fitStart 2, fitCenter 3, fitEnd 4, center 5, centerCrop 6, centerInside 7`.

### Retractions

| Registry ID | Old claim | Verdict |
|---|---|---|
| C1 | "no MeasureSpec layer exists" | `[F]` **WRONG** — `MeasureSpec2` + `M_UNSPEC` + `child_spec` exist in `layout_inflater.cpp` |
| E1 | "negative weight delta clamped away" | `[F]` **WRONG for the inflater engine** — `:4757` explicitly supports shrink |
| E2 | "weightSum never read" | `[F]` **WRONG** — `:1672`, `:2195`, `:4759` |
| G1 | "RelativeLayout anchor rules absent" | `[F]` **WRONG** — parsed and stored at `:2002-2004`. Whether they are *resolved into rects* is still open (see NEW-1) |
| H1/H2 | "GridLayout not implemented" | `[F]` **WRONG** — real Bellman-Ford arc solver at `:2898`, `:4364-4380` |
| I1/I3/I5 | "ScrollView never wired / bounded axis" | `[F]` **WRONG** — UNSPECIFIED both axes at `:3889`, `:3897` |
| E8 | "weighted children not re-measured" | `[F]` **WRONG** — `:4767` "Every weighted child is effectively re-measured with an EXACTLY spec (second pass)" |

**All of those observations remain true *of `renderer/view_renderer.cpp`*** — which is a separate, heuristic, MeasureSpec-free walk. So they are not deleted; they are **re-scoped** to the fallback engine.

### NEW-1 (P0, `[V]`) — Dual layout engines with divergent law sets

| | `resources/layout_inflater.cpp` | `renderer/view_renderer.cpp` |
|---|---|---|
| Lines | 5,713 | 1,094 |
| MeasureSpec | real (`MeasureSpec2`, `M_UNSPEC`, `child_spec`) | **none** (0 grep hits) |
| Weight law | AOSP sequential shares, negative excess, weightSum | one division, `max(0,free)`, no weightSum |
| GridLayout | Bellman-Ford arc solver | absent → FrameLayout |
| ScrollView | UNSPECIFIED both axes | `is_scroll()` defined, never called |
| RelativeLayout | rules parsed + stored | only parent/center flags |
| Gravity masking | to verify | frame path masked, linear/relative **raw bit tests** |
| Measure memo | yes, invalidated on dirty | none |

**This reframes the entire mission.** The user-visible symptom "9 grid cells stacked at the origin" is consistent with **the fallback engine running instead of the real one** — a *path-selection* defect, not a missing-law defect. Fixing laws in `view_renderer.cpp` would be wasted work if the real engine is supposed to run; conversely, if the fallback is what actually renders, then the honest port in `layout_inflater.cpp` is dead weight.

**Required next probe (assign to a coder, this is the top priority):**
1. Instrument both entry points and log which one produces the final `ViewNode` rects for a given APK.
2. Determine the selection predicate. The historical #606 gate `if (rt.loaded() || vs_dirty || inflated_attach_consumed)` in `execution_engine.cpp` is the prime suspect: an **XML-inflated** tree may reach the real engine while a **programmatically built** tree falls back to the heuristic walk. That would explain XML-vs-programmatic divergence exactly.
3. Publish the call graph `DEX → shadow → engine selection → rects → draw` with file:line for each hop.
4. Only then decide whether to (a) fix selection, or (b) delete the fallback and route everything through the honest port.

`[R]` AOSP references for the port that already exists — use these to validate it rather than rewrite it:
`LinearLayout.java` https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/refs/heads/master/core/java/android/widget/LinearLayout.java [[2]]
`GridLayout.java` https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/refs/heads/main/core/java/android/widget/GridLayout.java [[43]] · solver rationale https://android-developers.googleblog.com/2011/11/new-layout-widgets-space-and-gridlayout.html [[44]]
`RelativeLayout.java` https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/refs/heads/main/core/java/android/widget/RelativeLayout.java
`ScrollView.java` https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/refs/heads/main/core/java/android/widget/ScrollView.java

### NEW-2 (P1, `[V]`) — Tautological condition in the weight path
`layout_inflater.cpp:4751`
```cpp
if (is_ll && (horizontal || !is_scroll) && (horizontal || true)) {
```
`(horizontal || true)` is **always true**. Either dead scaffolding from a reverted experiment, or a lost condition. `clang-tidy misc-redundant-expression` / `-Wtautological-compare` class. Must be reduced to the intended predicate and covered by a test.

### NEW-3 (P1, `[V]`) — Weight stored as milli-units
`layout_inflater.cpp:4774` `weight_total += cn->layout_weight / 1000.0f;` paired with `real_layout.cpp:353` `n->layout_weight = (int)lround(rv.weight * 1000.0f)`.
Consistent, but **weights below 0.0005 quantize to zero**, and fractional weights accumulate rounding drift across many siblings. AOSP keeps `float weight`. Low severity, real.

### NEW-4 (P0, `[V]`) — Nine-patch absent from the bitmap decode path
`framework/bitmap_shadow.cpp` — 1,318 lines, `grep -iE 'nine.?patch|npTc|npLb'` → **0 hits**.
`resources/layout_inflater.cpp` — 5,713 lines, same grep → **1 hit, a comment** (`:2517` mentions `.9.png` as a path category only).
So the stretch-region / content-padding law has no implementation in either file. Consequence: nine-patch backgrounds do not stretch, and **nine-patch content padding is not applied** → Button/EditText text touches the drawable edge.
`[R]` Port from aapt2's own compiler (it defines the format you must read): https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/refs/heads/main/tools/aapt2/compile/Png.cpp [[11]] and `Image.h` — "9-patch content padding/insets … relative to the 9-patch NOT including the 1px thick source border" [[17]]. Authoring semantics: https://developer.android.com/studio/write/draw9patch [[13]]

### NEW-5 (P1, `[V]`) — `createScaledBitmap(filter=true)` silently does nearest-neighbour
`framework/bitmap_shadow.cpp:132` "Nearest-neighbour resample (createScaledBitmap; bilinear registered as …)"; `:785` logs a warning for `filter=true`; `:881` "bilinear honestly registered, same law as createScaledBitmap"; `:399` "Resample chain: raw → inSampleSize → density scale (nearest)".
AOSP `filter=true` means **bilinear**. The gap is honestly declared in comments, but it is a real visual defect (blocky upscaled assets, aliased downscales) and it compounds J2 in the renderer.
`[R]` `Bitmap.createScaledBitmap` contract: https://developer.android.com/reference/android/graphics/Bitmap#createScaledBitmap(android.graphics.Bitmap,%20int,%20int,%20boolean) · Skia sampling options: https://api.skia.org/structSkSamplingOptions.html

### RETRACTED — K3 was wrong
`inDensity` / `inTargetDensity` / `inScaled` / `inSampleSize` / `inJustDecodeBounds` / `inPreferredConfig` **are implemented with the AOSP laws** in `bitmap_shadow.cpp:200-353`, including `inSampleSize` `(dim + s - 1)/s` (`:200`, `:151`) and the `TypedValue.density → opts.inDensity` mapping (`:250-253`, `:329`). K3 is `[F]`.

### NEW-6 (P2, `[V]`) — GitHub code search does not index this repository
`GET /search/code?q=inPreferredConfig+repo:Sh-TB/MiniAndroid-Compatibility-Runtime+path:miniandroid/src` → `total_count: 0`, while the string demonstrably exists at `bitmap_shadow.cpp:325`. Same for `npTc`, `NinePatch`, `bilinear` (all 0).
**Operational consequence for every agent: never treat a zero-result GitHub code search on this repo as evidence of absence.** Absence must be proven by downloading the file and grepping locally. This is very likely a side effect of the 439 MB repo size (§A1) — another reason to strip the artifacts.

---

