## BATCH 4 — The live engine is a faithful AOSP port. NEW-11 and NEW-12 are FALSIFIED. The mission premise is largely wrong.

I ran the two probes I assigned in batch 3 against the **compiled** sources. Both came back clean. This is a negative result and it changes the mission's direction.

### NEW-11 → `[F]` FALSIFIED. Live gravity masking is CORRECT, including RTL.

`resources/layout_inflater.cpp` (manifest TU, 5,713 lines):
```cpp
// :4835  — the law is explicitly documented
// (HORIZONTAL = 0x7) then compare — a bare `& 0x5` test …
// :4980
// (VERTICAL = 0x70) then compare — a bare `& 0x50` test …

// :4864, :4983, :5376, :5658  — masked field extraction
int vf = vg & 0x70;
const int hf = vg & 0x7, vf = vg & 0x70;

// :5020-5027  — RTL flip, Gravity.getAbsoluteGravity
// relative-flag RTL flip (Gravity.getAbsoluteGravity):
if      (hf0 == 0x3) vg_eff = (vg_eff & ~0x7) | 0x5;
else if (hf0 == 0x5) vg_eff = (vg_eff & ~0x7) | 0x3;

// :5362-5371  — RELATIVE_LAYOUT_DIRECTION bit (0x00800000) handled
// :5663-5667  — FILL_HORIZONTAL / FILL_VERTICAL stretch
if (hf == 0x7)  w = std::max(0, inner_w);   // FILL
if (vf == 0x70) h = std::max(0, inner_h);
// :120-130    — XML token parse masks correctly on write
else if (tok == "center_horizontal") g = (g & ~0x7)  | 0x1;
else if (tok == "center_vertical")   g = (g & ~0x70) | 0x10;
else if (tok == "fill_vertical")     g |= 0x70;
// :1706 layoutDirection parsed · :4575 layoutDirection resolution walk
```
**Conclusion: D1/D2/D4/D5/D6 do not exist in the shipped runtime.** The 920 px gravity error table I published describes uncompiled code only. START/END, RTL, FILL and axis masking are all present and correct in the live path.

### §G → `[F]` FALSIFIED. Live RelativeLayout has the full AOSP dependency graph.

```cpp
// layout_inflater.cpp:3179
//   1. two dependency-sorted passes (horizontal, vertical) —
// :3192  "IllegalStateException: circular dependency in RelativeLayout";
// :3223-3225
// Kahn topological sort over one axis' anchor rules (AOSP
// DependencyGraph.getSortedViews). Self-dependency ignored
// (AOSP da3003 law); cycle → declaration order + diagnostic.
// :3251, :3580  "dependency — declaration order fallback"
// :3322-3327  START_OF/END_OF RTL aliasing
if (cn->rel_right_of_is_end) left_of_eff  = cn->rel_right_of_name;  // END_OF → LEFT_OF
if (cn->rel_left_of_is_start) right_of_eff = cn->rel_left_of_name;  // START_OF → RIGHT_OF
// :3417-3421 above/below anchors · :5185-5190 vertical placement from anchors
// :5230-5242 horizontal placement from anchors
```
G1–G6 are all dead-code-only. The live engine ports `DependencyGraph.getSortedViews` with Kahn's algorithm, per-axis passes, self-dependency tolerance and cycle fallback **with a diagnostic** — which is more careful than a naive port.

### NEW-12 → `[F]` FALSIFIED. All 8 scaleTypes are implemented in the live renderer.

`renderer/software_renderer.cpp:413-470` — `scale_image_rect(int scale_type, …)`, one function, full switch:

| ordinal | scaleType | lines | implementation |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | MATRIX | 421-424 | natural size at box origin (identity only) |
| 1 | FIT_XY | 425-428 | stretch to box |
| 2 | FIT_START | 429-433 | `min(bw/sw, bh/sh)`, aligned to origin |
| 3 | FIT_CENTER | 462-468 | fit scale, centered (also the `default`) |
| 4 | FIT_END | 434-439 | fit scale, aligned to far edge |
| 5 | CENTER | 440-444 | natural size, centered |
| 6 | CENTER_CROP | 445-453 | `max(bw/sw, bh/sh)`, centered |
| 7 | CENTER_INSIDE | 454-461 | `min(1, fit)`, centered |

Source-crop drawing also exists: `SoftwareCanvas::draw_image_region(src, sw, sh, sx, sy, sw, sh, dx, dy, dw, dh)` at `:496`. So J1/J2/J3/J12 are dead-code-only as well.

---

## What is actually left — real, live defects

### NEW-14 (P1, `[C]`) — CENTER / CENTER_CROP return rects that exceed the view box; clipping must be verified
`scale_image_rect` case 5 returns `r.w = src_w` even when `src_w > box_w`, and case 6 always returns a rect ≥ the box, with `r.x = box_x + (box_w - r.w)/2` which is **negative-offset** when `r.w > box_w`. AOSP clips the drawable to the ImageView bounds. If the caller of `scale_image_rect` does not push a clip rect, a CENTER/CENTER_CROP image will **paint outside its view** — the exact "images incorrectly scaled, cropped, or positioned" symptom.
**Probe:** find every call site of `scale_image_rect` and confirm a clip to `(box_x, box_y, box_w, box_h)` is active. This is a 10-minute check with a decisive answer.
`[R]` `ImageView.configureBounds()` + `Canvas.clipRect` semantics: https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/refs/heads/main/core/java/android/widget/ImageView.java [[62]] · golden visual references for CENTER vs CENTER_CROP [[57]] [[64]]

### NEW-15 (P1, `[V]`) — nearest-neighbour sampling justified by an app-specific assumption
`software_renderer.cpp:477-479`:
```cpp
// Uses nearest-neighbour sampling for scaling — no fancy interpolation,
// because the source PNGs we care about (simplestopwatch icons) are tiny
// and need to render at their natural size anyway.
```
A framework primitive is being scoped by one corpus app's asset profile. Any app that upscales a photo or downscales a banner gets blocky/aliased output. Combined with NEW-5 (`createScaledBitmap(filter=true)` also nearest), **the entire image pipeline has no bilinear path**.
**Fix:** implement bilinear in `draw_image_region` and honour `filter=true` in `bitmap_shadow.cpp`. Use Skia's sampling semantics as the reference.
`[R]` https://api.skia.org/structSkSamplingOptions.html · `Bitmap.createScaledBitmap` filter contract https://developer.android.com/reference/android/graphics/Bitmap#createScaledBitmap(android.graphics.Bitmap,%20int,%20int,%20boolean)

### NEW-16 (P1, `[V]`) — hard measure-depth cap of 100
`layout_inflater.cpp:3005-3008`:
```cpp
// shallow; a cycle here (inflater bug) must fail loudly instead of …
fprintf(stderr, "[U007-LAYOUT] ERROR: measure depth > 100 at view %u (%s) — cycle suspected\n", …);
```
AOSP has no fixed depth limit; deeply nested but **valid** trees (RecyclerView item trees, Compose interop, deep ConstraintLayout chains) can exceed 100. The guard conflation is "deep == cyclic". Make the cap configurable, and detect cycles by visited-set on the (view, spec) path rather than by depth.

### NEW-17 (P2, `[V]`) — MATRIX scaleType ignores the actual matrix
`:421-424` implements MATRIX as identity at box origin. Apps that call `setImageMatrix()` (custom top-crop viewers, zoom/pan galleries) will render unscaled at the origin. `framework/matrix_shadow.cpp` is a manifest TU, so the matrix state exists — it is simply not consumed here.
`[R]` Community top-crop MATRIX pattern that real apps ship: https://gist.github.com/arriolac/3843346 [[63]] · https://stackoverflow.com/questions/6330084/imageview-scaling-top-crop [[56]]

---

## Honest reassessment of the mission premise

The mission brief asserts "margins, padding, gravity, weights, and alignment do not reliably match Android behavior" and asks for the missing laws to be found. **After reading the compiled engine, that premise is largely false.** `layout_inflater.cpp` contains an honest, well-documented AOSP port covering:

- real MeasureSpec (`MeasureSpec2`, `M_UNSPEC`) + `child_spec` with padding/margin subtraction
- measure memoisation invalidated on `layout_dirty`
- LinearLayout sequential weight shares with **negative excess (shrink)** and explicit `weightSum`
- GridLayout **Bellman-Ford arc constraint solver** (not a table)
- RelativeLayout **Kahn topological sort per axis** + cycle fallback + START_OF/END_OF RTL aliasing
- ScrollView **and** HorizontalScrollView UNSPECIFIED main axis
- gravity axis masking + `getAbsoluteGravity` RTL flip + FILL
- all 8 ImageView scaleTypes + source-region drawing
- BitmapFactory `inDensity`/`inTargetDensity`/`inScaled`/`inSampleSize`/`inJustDecodeBounds`/`inPreferredConfig`
- SRC-OVER compositing with a premultiplied layer mode
- libpng / libjpeg / libwebp / stb_image GIF89a / rlottie decoders

**Therefore the remaining visual defects are much more likely to be:**
1. **Path selection / traversal timing** — a frame where the `:3816` gate is false reuses stale geometry. `frame_census_.layout_source` (NEW-13) is the instrument that answers this definitively.
2. **Missing drawable features** — nine-patch (NEW-4, verified absent), bilinear (NEW-5/NEW-15), MATRIX (NEW-17).
3. **Clipping** — CENTER/CENTER_CROP overflow (NEW-14).
4. **Resource resolution** — reference/theme chains and config selection in `arsc_parser.cpp` / `resource_runtime.cpp` (still unaudited).
5. **Text** — `text_shaper.cpp` (still unaudited); Persian/Arabic shaping is the highest-risk unknown.
6. **Process defects that cause wasted work** — 5.74 MB of divergent dead code (NEW-7) and a 439 MB repo (A1).

**Recommendation to the main coder: re-scope LAYOUT-GEOMETRY-001.** Do not commission "implement GridLayout / RelativeLayout / ScrollView / weights" — they exist. Commission instead: (a) prove which engine and which traversal produced a given framebuffer using `layout_source`, (b) delete the dead engines, (c) close the four concrete gaps above.

